# EAS falls back to `yarn install` when no npm lockfile is present, and yarn 1
# treats the `engines` field as a hard error. Several Solana wallet-standard
# deps declare `node >=22`, but the EAS Android builder runs Node 20. These are
# runtime (Hermes) deps, not build tooling, so the builder's Node version is
# irrelevant to them — tell yarn to skip the engine check instead of failing.
--ignore-engines true
